module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_cast_admitted_from_a_carrier_refused_from_its_refined_alias

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { NoRungStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

// A cast the compiler refuses although it admits every step of it, filed from a measurement rather than
// inferred. Census run 41768647568 holds the refusals; the admitting legs are pinned by code that
// compiles on main, quoted with their file:line in the receipts. The repair is a compiler-side verdict,
// named in the last receipt, and is not the change that files this row.
data a_cast_admitted_from_a_carrier_refused_from_its_refined_alias: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_cast_admitted_from_a_carrier_refused_from_its_refined_alias" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: NoRungStated },

  receipts: [
    "**A TWO-LEG CAST IS REFUSED AS A COMPOSITE ALTHOUGH THE COMPILER ADMITS EACH LEG, AND THE REFUSAL NAMES THE LEG THAT IS ADMITTED** (INVALID STATE: `text as Secret` is admitted, where Secret is a nominal_opaque whose carrier is String; `branded_text as String` is admitted, eliminating a brand to its carrier; `branded_text as Secret` - the composition of exactly those two - refuses at the emit stage, and the diagnostic it prints names the intermediate pair, NonEmptyStr to String, which is one of the legs already admitted. v1.compiler.emit cast_realization_refusal_fact, src/v1/05_emit.dag:3517, builds that text from whatever pair the walk stalled on, so the sentence indicts a crossing that compiles elsewhere in the same corpus).",
    "HARM. The answer cannot be derived from the corpus's own precedents, and it points the reader at the wrong half of the path. Read literally it says the text is unreachable, which invites the reader to carry a SECOND representation of the value beside the branded one so a site has something to cast - two sources for one value, drifting the moment either is written on its own, and the brand stops being the thing identity is taken from. That is the repair this row forbids: it was nearly taken here, on five sites in two modules, and review 90521 on gunbc#15775 stopped it before it landed.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. This is not the ungrounded-cast class, where an unidentified source or a type variable reaches no verdict at all: here both endpoints are named, both legs are decided, and only the composite is refused. It is also not a missing route: the route exists at std.types.secret_of_text, and taking it is what the sites now do - secret_of_text(jwt as String), an admitted elimination followed by a named entry, with no chained `as` into a nominal (DESIGN 5 names chaining past a refusal as the workaround tell, and the two-hop jwt as String as Secret was proposed and rejected on exactly that ground). The recognition rule is a question to ask of any such refusal, before routing around it: does the pair the diagnostic names appear, admitted, anywhere else in the corpus? Here the answer is yes, three times over, in code that compiles today.",
    "WHAT IS ADMITTED, WITH ITS RECEIPTS. String onto Secret: dag/extdeps/shell/credentials.dag:30 does text as Secret in env_credential_token, on a live chain through gunbc.org_actions_inspection and extdeps.github.auth, and grep -rn 'as Secret' --include=*.dag dag/ src/ counts 148 spellings at this head (an upper bound: it matches comments and strings too). Branded text onto String: dag/test/claim/github_effect_perform_witness.dag:51 compares a JwtCompactSerialization - dag/extdeps/auth/jws.dag:108, a NonEmptyStr carrying a brand - with `as String`, and extdeps.auth.jws.jws_compact_serialization does signing_input as String on a plain NonEmptyStr, and the witness at :114 does it to EncodedJitConfig.encoded, declared encoded: NonEmptyStr at dag/extdeps/github/actions_jit_runner.dag:68. All three compile on main.",
    "WHAT WAS REFUSED, WITH ITS RECEIPT (2026-11-04, clever-carp-493, census run 41768647568). jwt as Secret at dag/gunbc/github_effect_perform.dag:239:26, :658:65, :688:63 and dag/gunbc/auth/github_app_control_plane_observe.dag:168:120, :180:119 - five sites, each printing 'cast cannot be emitted for target rust -- no declared conversion route from NonEmptyStr to String'. The census that measured them is the mirror CI head; it cannot be re-run at main's head until the drift-route PR lands, because main's committed drift-watch step dies at an unrelated TypeError before the emit stage.",
    "WHERE THE REPAIR BELONGS. At the grounded-cast layer, where a composite should be judged by the verdicts of its legs rather than stalling mid-path: v1.compiler.infer grounded_cast_verdict, src/v1/04_infer.dag:8295, is the one home for that judgement and it already answers Admitted for each leg here. It is the same region as the ungrounded-cast class whose verdict reaches no consumer, so it travels with that work and with the stage0 mirror catch-up; it is not a lane open from a worktree. No control here goes red when the composite regrows, which is why the rung is stated as unread rather than claimed: this filing changes what five sites write and what the reader is told, and executes nothing.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.types", decl_name: "secret_of_text", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.auth.jws", decl_name: "jws_compact_serialization", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.github_effect_perform", decl_name: "JitMintAppJwt", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "grounded_cast_verdict", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.emit", decl_name: "cast_realization_refusal_fact", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
